{"type":"text","timestamp":"2026-09-18T13:38:11.042Z","data":{"text":"Task 5 is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented write-only checkbox projection for passed task verification.\n\n**Changed**\n- `src/watcher/runner.ts`: replaced the single-regex `tickTaskCheckbox` with an exported pure helper `tickTaskCheckboxContent(content, taskNumber)` and a thin file writer. It now ticks:\n  - flat numbered checklists (`- [ ] 3. ...`)\n  - grouped checklists with numbered items\n  - grouped checklists with unnumbered items whose number is on the `## <n>.` section header\n  \n  It preserves original numbering punctuation/spacing, is idempotent, no-ops on a missing `tasks.md`, and never touches `.run/`.\n- `tests/runner-checkbox-projection.test.ts` (new, 11 tests): format handling, on-disk tick, approval-hash preservation, `.run/` marker immutability, two guards that state derives only from `.run/` (source-level and functional), the runner verify-pass path (`.run/done/1` + ticked checkbox), and full-tick verification of the 15 archived `tasks.md` files.\n\n**Verification**\n- Task verify: `node --import tsx --test tests/runner-checkbox-projection.test.ts` → 11/11 pass\n- Repo gate: `pnpm verify` → 389/389 tests, `tsc --noEmit` clean, `biome check` clean\n\n**Notable decision**: `*`-bullet items are intentionally not ticked because `hasher.normalizeTasksMd` only canonicalizes `-` bullets; ticking them would change the hash. That fix would require out-of-scope `hasher.ts`. The archive check asserts `>= 15` fully-ticked files to stay valid as future changes archive.\n\nResult written to `specs/016-openspec-artifacts/.run/results/5.md`."}}
